Drop the dbus-glib dependency, which nothing uses.

meson.build asks for dbus-glib-1 and links the greeter with it, but no
source file includes a dbus-glib header or calls into it (the greeter
talks to LightDM through liblightdm-gobject, which uses GDBus).  dbus-glib
is a deprecated library, and requiring it means porting it for nothing.

Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -17,7 +17,6 @@
 # ------->>> Dependency Checks <<<------- #
 # ======================================= #
 
-dbus_glib       = dependency('dbus-glib-1')
 lightdm_gobject = dependency('liblightdm-gobject-1')
 x11             = dependency('x11')
 
@@ -25,7 +24,7 @@
 webkit2         = dependency('webkit2gtk-4.1',               version: '>=2.12')
 webkit2_webext  = dependency('webkit2gtk-web-extension-4.1', version: '>=2.12')
 
-greeter_deps = [dbus_glib, gtk3, webkit2, x11]
+greeter_deps = [gtk3, webkit2, x11]
 webext_deps = [webkit2_webext, lightdm_gobject]
 
 has_webkitgtk_2_14   = webkit2.version().version_compare('>=2.14')
